          "text": "Dear Colleague,\n\n**History of Present Illness:**  \nThe patient has focal epilepsy with focal-to-bilateral tonic-clonic seizures. Seizure onset occurred at age 25 years. Current seizure frequency is approximately 7 seizures per week.\n\n**Current Antiseizure Medications:**  \n- Topiramate  \n- Brivaracetam  \n- Carbamazepine  \n- Zonisamide  \n\n**Seizure Burden:**  \nApproximately 7 focal-to-bilateral tonic-clonic seizures per week despite the current antiseizure medication regimen.\n\n**Assessment:**  \nDrug-resistant focal epilepsy of structural etiology. MRI demonstrates focal cortical dysplasia.\n\n**Plan:**  \nTopiramate, brivaracetam, carbamazepine, and zonisamide remain the current antiseizure medications. Continue clinical management of drug-resistant structural focal epilepsy.",
